Z||000000||DISenchanted||09-14-1999||01:25 PM||||Last night I floored my car for the first time.  I recently purchased the car and have been fixing it up slowly.  I was at a light and this little honda with Juan Valdez exhaust starts reving his hamster.  When the light turns green I floor it and the car takes off, leaving the little rice burner in the dust. At about 4500 rpm I decide to shift because it wasn't even a challenge.  I let off the gas and I keep accelerating.  At about 5900 I turn the car off, then tun the key back so I wouln't loose my steering.  I pull over and nothing looks wrong. I get back in and the car is fine.  As long as I don't floor it.  Any I deas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dale||09-14-1999||01:48 PM||||Bummer,<BR>stuck throttle, check around to see if it might be catching on something from the carpet to the throttle body.  You might also put a heavier return spring on it.  also check for rust and or corosion that might have built up around the linkage.  WD40||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||09-14-1999||04:33 PM||||That must have been scary...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Fortunately you had the presence of mind to turn off the ignition (and turn it back on again so it wouldn't fall into its lock).<P>My girlfiend sometimes drives my car and I'm always afraid something like that will happen...||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-14-1999||08:20 PM||||replace the TPS. It may be binding. Even if it's not, you can clean under it, and then you know it's good. Odds are it's about worn out anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||09-14-1999||09:24 PM||||Turn off the auto-go-fast switch!!<P>Glad your ok. I`ve heard of this before on a fiero. It was the cable. Replace it!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||09-15-1999||09:05 AM||||I hope I don't open myself up for membership in the "dumbass-of-the-month" club for admitting this...<P>When I bought my first Fiero, the throttle would occasionally stick partially or completely open, scaring the begeezus out of me.  I started at the pedal and worked my way back to the TBI, lubing everything and finding no problem.  After all this, I finally realized it was the factory floor mat jamming under the pedal.  I drilled two holes in it and sandwiched it between the seat mounting bracket and the floor.  End of problem.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dale||09-15-1999||01:46 PM||||Hey Chadman, don't feel stupid, Thats why I posted the message that I did.  It happened to me to.||||reg||6
